      "summary": "Man&#039;s ceremonial sword belt; tablet woven and made from two shades of blue (indigo dyed?) cotton yarn; padded (save for 23 cms at fringed end).  Three sections of identical Islamic inscription in Kufic (?) calligraphy.  One end has long loop; the other very long fringes.  Floral patterning within rectangle on reverse, with alternating reverse colourway, separated by four bands. Appears that entirely separate patterns made at the same time, as same weft used for both sides; if so, a great technical feat.",
